{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_5","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/bash -lc \"python3 - <<'PY'\nfrom pathlib import Path\nimport json\nimport hashlib\n\nbase = Path('../research/skill-drafts')\nmanifest = json.loads((base / 'frozen-artifact-manifest.json').read_text())\nexpected = {item['path']: item['sha256'] for item in manifest['files']}\nassert len(expected) == len(manifest['files']), 'Duplicate manifest paths'\nnames = sorted({Path(path).parts[0] for path in expected})\nassert len(names) == 5, 'Expected exactly five skills'\ncache_names = {'__pycache__', '.pytest_cache', '.mypy_cache', '.ruff_cache', '.cache'}\nactual = set()\nskipped = []\nfor name in names:\n    assert not Path(name).exists(), f'Destination already exists: {name}'\n    for path in (base / name).rglob('*'):\n        relative = path.relative_to(base)\n        assert not path.is_symlink(), f'Unexpected symlink: {relative}'\n        if any(part in cache_names for part in relative.parts) or path.suffix in {'.pyc', '.pyo'}:\n            if path.is_file():\n                skipped.append(str(relative))\n            continue\n        if path.is_file():\n            actual.add(str(relative))\nassert actual == set(expected), f'Manifest tree mismatch: missing={set(expected)-actual}, extra={actual-set(expected)}'\nfor relative, digest in expected.items():\n    assert hashlib.sha256((base / relative).read_bytes()).hexdigest() == digest, f'Source SHA256 mismatch: {relative}'\nprint(json.dumps({'skills': names, 'verified_source_files': len(expected), 'excluded_cache_files': skipped}, indent=2))\nfor name in names:\n    print(f'--- {name}/SKILL.md ---')\n    print((base / name / 'SKILL.md').read_text())\nPY\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_5","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/bash -lc \"python3 - <<'PY'\nfrom pathlib import Path\nimport json\nimport hashlib\n\nbase = Path('../research/skill-drafts')\nmanifest = json.loads((base / 'frozen-artifact-manifest.json').read_text())\nexpected = {item['path']: item['sha256'] for item in manifest['files']}\nassert len(expected) == len(manifest['files']), 'Duplicate manifest paths'\nnames = sorted({Path(path).parts[0] for path in expected})\nassert len(names) == 5, 'Expected exactly five skills'\ncache_names = {'__pycache__', '.pytest_cache', '.mypy_cache', '.ruff_cache', '.cache'}\nactual = set()\nskipped = []\nfor name in names:\n    assert not Path(name).exists(), f'Destination already exists: {name}'\n    for path in (base / name).rglob('*'):\n        relative = path.relative_to(base)\n        assert not path.is_symlink(), f'Unexpected symlink: {relative}'\n        if any(part in cache_names for part in relative.parts) or path.suffix in {'.pyc', '.pyo'}:\n            if path.is_file():\n                skipped.append(str(relative))\n            continue\n        if path.is_file():\n            actual.add(str(relative))\nassert actual == set(expected), f'Manifest tree mismatch: missing={set(expected)-actual}, extra={actual-set(expected)}'\nfor relative, digest in expected.items():\n    assert hashlib.sha256((base / relative).read_bytes()).hexdigest() == digest, f'Source SHA256 mismatch: {relative}'\nprint(json.dumps({'skills': names, 'verified_source_files': len(expected), 'excluded_cache_files': skipped}, indent=2))\nfor name in names:\n    print(f'--- {name}/SKILL.md ---')\n    print((base / name / 'SKILL.md').read_text())\nPY\"","aggregated_output":"{\n  \"skills\": [\n    \"align-with-stamped-principles\",\n    \"assess-alignment-with-stamped-principles\",\n    \"create-repronim-stamped-project\",\n    \"create-stamped-project\",\n    \"do-full-research-loop\"\n  ],\n  \"verified_source_files\": 20,\n  \"excluded_cache_files\": []\n}\n--- align-with-stamped-principles/SKILL.md ---\n---\nname: align-with-stamped-principles\ndescription: Improve an existing project's STAMPED alignment using a scoped baseline assessment, concrete changes, and evidence-based reassessment. Use when asked to add STAMPED or improve a research object's reproducibility practices.\nversion: 0.1.0\n---\n\n# Align an existing research object\n\nStart from the project's intended use and existing stack. Read\n[the principles orientation](references/principles.md), consult pinned paper\nand checklist sources, and inspect the actual object before changing it.\n\nIf available, use assess-alignment-with-stamped-principles for the baseline.\nOtherwise record the same essential information directly: exact object\nsnapshot and boundary; use case and assumptions; each principle's observed\nimplementation, evidence, judgment, uncertainty, and relevant gap. Inspecting\ninstructions is different from executing them. Keep unknowns visible and\nscientific validity separate from research-object quality.\n\nChoose changes for this use case. For a static dataset, access, metadata,\ncomponent identities and modularity may dominate; for transformations, explicit\nexecution and disposable environments may be essential. Keep normative\nrequirements distinct from the project's priorities and tradeoffs.\n\nExplain what will change, which gap it addresses, and how success will be\nchecked. Perform authorized, scoped, reversible improvements without adding\nan unnecessary approval round. Preserve the project's chosen tooling and\nworking instruction hierarchy. Introduce another tool only when it addresses\na demonstrated gap better than the existing mechanism. Do not make STAMPED\nsynonymous with a particular package manager, data manager, or hosting service.\n\nTypical changes are a missing component manifest, exact source identities,\nexplicit inputs/outputs, a replay entry point, tracked environment definition,\ndocumented host configuration, or an accessible distribution route. Prefer\nan executable improvement with evidence over a promise in documentation.\nRetain limitations when the ideal is impractical.\n\nWhen useful, add concise guidance to the existing agent harness at the proper\nscope: object boundary, established execution and provenance route, where\nthe environment is defined, and how to verify results. Preserve existing\nAGENTS.md/CLAUDE.md or other conventions and avoid duplicating their content.\nDo not install a skill dependency or write global account configuration merely\nto add a pointer. Recommend optional complementary skills only for actual gaps.\n\nReassess the resulting snapshot using the original criteria. Link each claimed\nimprovement to a diff and observed check; distinguish implemented and verified,\nimplemented but unverified, planned, blocked, and deferred work. Preserve\nfailed attempts. Loop again only for concrete newly discovered defects within\nscope; stop when the requested improvements are verified or the remaining\nbarrier is documented with a useful next action. Deliver the before/after\nassessment and the executable result, not just revised agent instructions.\n\n--- assess-alignment-with-stamped-principles/SKILL.md ---\n---\nname: assess-alignment-with-stamped-principles\ndescription: Assess an existing project, dataset, workflow, or research object against STAMPED for its documented use case, retaining criterion-level evidence and checklist responses. Use for assessment; use an alignment workflow when changes are requested.\nversion: 0.1.0\n---\n\n# Assess STAMPED alignment\n\nAssess the specified object and exact snapshot, not the reputation of its\ntools. Establish its intended use, audience, boundary, components, and relevant\nconstraints from documentation and the user. Distinguish the software that\nproduces research objects from an actual produced object. Do not infer an\nundocumented scientific objective merely from filenames. Record unresolved\ngoals as assumptions or questions while inspecting what is available.\n\nRead [the principles orientation](references/principles.md), then consult the\npaper and checklist at pinned revisions. Prefer an existing project reference\nbundle for longitudinal comparison; report newer-source differences separately.\nUse current normative statements without converting SHOULD/MAY guidance into\nuniversal requirements. An operational summary is not a replacement paper.\n\n## Collect evidence proportional to the claim\n\nDefine observable criteria and scope before scoring. Use the checklist's\nstable item IDs and exact version; add use-case criteria when needed. Record\npriority, intended direction (maximize, balance, preserve), rationale, and\nrequired evidence-gathering activities. Lower priority does not erase an\nunmet normative requirement.\n\nInspect instructions, component identities, environment definitions,\ntransformation records, module interfaces, access/license conditions, and\nretained outputs. Resolve references, retrieve data, construct environments,\nexecute, compare, or independently reproduce when the task and resources\nauthorize those checks. A read-only review does not authorize executing\narbitrary project commands. State the coverage actually achieved.\n\nKeep observations distinct from judgments. An attempted operation can finish\nand reveal a failure; a missing attempt is not an observed access barrier.\nUse demonstrated, partial, not_demonstrated, unknown, or not_applicable with\ncriterion-specific reasons and evidence. Require the planned evidence for a\npositive judgment. A successful command, lockfile, container, or repository\nalone proves no other property. Ephemerality concerns computation, not\ndiscarding valuable results. Access restrictions need intended-recipient\ncontext before concluding that distribution is impossible.\n\n## Return reusable evidence\n\nProduce a seven-property table: criterion, observed implementation/evidence,\njudgment, uncertainty, remaining gap, and smallest relevant next step. Preserve\nall checklist items, marking unassessed items unknown and justified exclusions\nnot_applicable. Do not aggregate principles into an unqualified compliance\nscore. Keep scientific correctness separate from research-object quality.\n\nUse [the assessment contract](references/assessment-contract.md) and\n[the schema](references/research-assessment.schema.json) for a portable JSON\nrecord, or the project's established schema with an explicit field crosswalk.\nInclude the skill version and exact source snapshot/digest, assessor identity,\nreference versions, observed activities, conditions, evidence, and gaps.\nDistinguish unreviewed agent assertions from independent human/agent reviews.\nCorrections become new records that supersede the old record.\n\nEmit a checklist-compatible side product following\n[the checklist response reference](references/checklist-responses.md).\nKeep rich judgments and evidence in the assessment; the UI's yes/no/null and\nshort reason field cannot represent all states. Use the bundled export helper\nonly with a pinned checklist and the reviewed per-item answers. Report source\nversion conflicts rather than silently translating incompatible criteria.\n\nAssessment does not imply mutation. When changes are requested, hand off the\nevidence and priorities to an alignment workflow, then reassess the resulting\nsnapshot with the same criteria and explicit additions.\n\n--- create-repronim-stamped-project/SKILL.md ---\n---\nname: create-repronim-stamped-project\ndescription: Create a neuroimaging research project using a ReproNim-oriented adapter for STAMPED, including BIDS-aware organization, versioned data, reproducible environments, and captured execution. Use for an explicitly ReproNim-oriented project.\nversion: 0.1.0\n---\n\n# Apply a ReproNim adapter\n\nPreserve the scientific question and the user's tool choices. Read\n[the principles orientation](references/principles.md) and\n[the implementation reference](references/repronim.md). Distinguish the\nprinciples from this adapter's practical defaults.\n\nPrepare a creation brief containing the question, audience, data permissions,\nbudget, exact source identities, BIDS/raw-versus-derivative boundaries,\nenvironment/runtime requirements, provenance strategy, and expected checks.\nUse create-stamped-project if available. Otherwise perform its essential\nworkflow directly: establish the object boundary; create explicit components,\nenvironment and execution entry point; run the smallest complete slice;\nretain evidence; assess all seven properties and unresolved gaps.\n\nPrefer DataLad/git-annex for versioned datasets and transformations and a\nproject-local declared environment such as Pixi where compatible with the\nproject. Retain upstream datasets as independently identified subdatasets\nwhen that is their natural distribution. Pin content and container digests;\nrecord where bytes can actually be obtained. A Git commit or annex key alone\ndoes not guarantee retrieval.\n\nHonor the BIDS version and relevant derivative specification for the chosen\nmodality. Preserve source metadata and licenses, keep raw inputs immutable,\nand put generated data/figures in a clearly identified derivative or analysis\nmodule. Record subject/session/run selection and exclusions. BIDS validity\ndoes not establish appropriateness of the scientific analysis.\n\nFor BIDS Apps, prefer the user's configured orchestration, using MechaBABS when\nrequested. Inspect its installed version, configuration, and official usage;\ndo not invent commands. Verify one inexpensive job including output collection\nand provenance before scaling. Record scheduler limits and measured pilot\nresource use. Do not add a container, remote cluster, or imaging pipeline for\na question answerable with simpler data.\n\nLink native agent history, execution/resource logs, and DataLad transformation\nrecords with shared run identifiers while keeping their meanings distinct.\nApply the project's capture prerequisites to each delegated repository or\nworktree. A disposable environment should leave durable analysis results,\nsource identities, and logs.\n\nVerify fresh retrieval and a bounded replay where feasible. Report scientific\nvalidity separately from the seven STAMPED properties, scope checks to observed\nplatforms and access conditions, and expose remaining limitations. Tools named\nhere implement choices; their presence is not evidence of successful alignment.\n\n--- create-stamped-project/SKILL.md ---\n---\nname: create-stamped-project\ndescription: Establish a new computational research project with an explicit research-object boundary, component identities, executable workflow, environment specification, and proportionate STAMPED checks. Use for project creation without imposing a domain-specific tool stack.\nversion: 0.1.0\n---\n\n# Create a STAMPED-informed project\n\nRead [the principles orientation](references/principles.md), then consult and\npin the paper and checklist sources. Establish the user's objective, audience,\ndata/access constraints, expected outputs, collaborators, computational scale,\nand chosen tools. Inspect supplied examples and the relevant workspace before\nasking for missing facts. Prior conversation or shell history is contextual\nevidence only when authorized and relevant; do not broadly mine private history\nor turn old messages into new authorization.\n\nChoose the smallest structure that makes the work understandable and\nexecutable. Explain the research-object root, input and output boundaries,\nmodule responsibilities, environment definition, provenance mechanism, and\nretrieval/distribution route. Modules may be directly included or persistently\nreferenced. A particular directory tree, version-control implementation,\ncontainer runtime, or package manager is not a STAMPED requirement.\n\nCreate useful working content: a question/use-case record, an inventory of\nessential inputs and their exact identities/access/license terms, the analysis\nentry point or smallest runnable slice, a tracked environment definition, and\noutput and provenance locations. Mark unresolved inputs explicitly; do not\nclaim a runnable study while indispensable data or credentials are missing.\nKeep generated outputs outside raw inputs and private access materials outside\nshareable content. Record host requirements rather than assuming a laptop's\nambient state.\n\nUse the existing project conventions for agent instructions. Add only the\nspecific boundary, setup, execution, provenance, and validation facts future\nwork needs. A generic manifesto is not a substitute for a working entry point.\n\nVerify the smallest complete operation from declared inputs through retained\noutputs and a replay recipe. Check restoration in a fresh disposable workspace\nwhen feasible; preserve the result and logs before removing the workspace.\nDo not claim cross-platform portability from a single-host run.\n\nFinish with a baseline assessment across all seven properties, citing observed\nevidence and separating gaps, unknowns, and deliberate tradeoffs. If the\nalignment skill is available, use it with the actual use case and structure;\notherwise apply its essential loop directly: assess, choose a scoped fix,\nimplement, check, and reassess. When the user asked for the completed study,\ncontinue through analysis and reporting using an execution workflow rather\nthan stopping at project setup.\n\n--- do-full-research-loop/SKILL.md ---\n---\nname: do-full-research-loop\ndescription: Carry out a specified computational research study from question and data through analysis, verification, replay, and an evidence-linked report. Use when the user asks to execute a study end to end; preserve a planning-only request's scope.\nversion: 0.1.0\n---\n\n# Execute the research loop\n\nProduce the requested scientific result and an inspectable research object.\nWhen execution is requested, a plan or scaffold is an intermediate product.\nUse the project's chosen tools; this skill requires no particular package\nmanager, provenance system, repository host, or execution service.\n\nRead [the principles orientation](references/principles.md). Consult and pin\nthe current paper and checklist before making STAMPED judgments. If the\nproject already pins a reference bundle, retain it for comparable assessments\nand record newer-source differences separately.\n\n## Establish an executable study\n\nExtract the question, intended audience, permitted data, deliverables, resource\nlimits, and stopping conditions from the request and project. Identify which\nfacts are documented and which are assumptions. Resolve only missing facts\nthat change the scientific question or authorization; continue independent\nwork while waiting. If question selection is delegated, choose a feasible\nquestion and record why its data and method can answer it.\n\nBefore analysis, retain a concise protocol: population/sample, unit of\nanalysis, variables and units, missingness/exclusions, estimand or descriptive\ntarget, method, uncertainty, anticipated confounders, and validity checks.\nExploratory changes remain allowed, but record their timing and rationale;\ndo not relabel them as prespecified or select results for significance.\n\nIdentify the research-object boundary and capture exact data, code, environment,\nparameter, and instruction identities. Retain retrieval routes and terms as\nwell as hashes. Give every computation explicit inputs and outputs and a\ntracked executable entry point. Establish the project's existing provenance\nand agent-history capture before delegating work. Link native agent history,\ncomputational logs, and transformation provenance by trial/run identifiers;\neach establishes different evidence and none substitutes for the others.\n\n## Run, inspect, and extend\n\n1. Check access and semantics on the smallest useful slice. Verify columns,\n   units, sample counts, dependencies, and the output contract before scaling.\n2. Execute the pilot. Inspect its scientific outputs, resource use, exit\n   status, and provenance. A process finishing successfully does not establish\n   valid science. Diagnose failed attempts and retain their inputs, errors,\n   interventions, and partial results distinctly from accepted outputs.\n3. Complete the planned study within the recorded limits. Reuse a proven\n   entry point; keep input versions fixed within a trial. Do not expand into\n   a larger dataset or expensive pipeline merely because capacity exists.\n   Choose a concrete retry bound before an uncertain batch. When it is\n   exhausted, change the justified approach, reduce scope transparently, or\n   report the barrier; do not repeat an unchanged failing action.\n4. Test the claim with checks appropriate to the method: independent summary\n   calculations, expected ranges, denominator and exclusion audits, simulated\n   known cases, or sensitivity analyses. Distinguish technical validity from\n   generalizability, causal interpretation, and external scientific truth.\n5. Replay from recorded inputs and environment definitions in a fresh\n   disposable workspace. Compare prespecified outputs using exact digests\n   for deterministic artifacts or declared numerical/semantic tolerances.\n   A rerun in the original directory is useful but does not establish clean\n   restoration, cross-platform portability, or independent reproduction.\n\nKeep the work moving through these stages. Only pause dependent work for a\nreal authorization/access dependency or a scientific ambiguity that cannot be\nresolved honestly. Retain the useful completed result if some stage is blocked.\n\n## Deliver and assess\n\nDeliver the executable analysis, results/figures, source identities,\nenvironment definition, replay instructions and observed replay outcome,\nand a concise evidence-linked interpretation with limits and unresolved gaps.\nPreserve computational evidence before disposable environments are removed.\nSharing an artifact is a separate action from preparing it; follow the user's\nactual publication scope.\n\nUse [the assessment contract](references/assessment-contract.md) and\n[the JSON Schema](references/research-assessment.schema.json) for a structured\nassessment when requested or when this is a skill-evaluation study. Report\nscientific validity and the seven STAMPED properties separately. A reproducible\nmistake remains a scientific mistake. A correct number can have an unusable\nresearch object. Neither becomes a universal score.\n\nFor comparisons with and without a skill, read\n[the comparison protocol](references/paired-evaluation.md) before starting\neither arm. Do not invent use, outcome, timing, or token measurements. One\nexploratory pair illustrates behavior under its conditions; it does not\nestablish general skill efficacy.\n\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
